  "name": "Reply to support emails in the same thread with an AI agent, OpenAI and SendRaven",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "e66caf29-0547-598a-b17f-48ab599ef627",
      "name": "About this workflow",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1000,
        -300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 540,
        "height": 780,
        "content": "## Reply to support emails in the same thread with an AI agent\n\nA customer emails your support address. The agent reads the whole conversation and answers **in the same email thread** from your own domain, or leaves it for a person.\n\n### How it works\n1. SendRaven posts each received email to the webhook, signed with HMAC-SHA256.\n2. The signature and timestamp are checked, the webhook is answered at once, and retries already processed are dropped.\n3. Auto-replies such as out-of-office are skipped.\n4. The full thread is loaded, so the agent sees earlier messages too.\n5. The agent chooses **reply**, **no reply needed** (thread marked handled) or **escalate** (it stays in your unanswered list).\n6. The reply is threaded with `reply_to_message_id`. Its Idempotency-Key comes from the received email, so a retry never sends it twice.\n\n### Setup\n1. Sign up at [sendraven.ai](https://sendraven.ai/?utm_source=n8n&utm_medium=template&utm_campaign=sendraven_launch) and verify a domain, including the inbound MX record shown under **Receiving replies**.\n2. Create an API key with **emails:send** and **threads:read**, ticking **Hold every send for human approval** while testing. Save it as a **Bearer Auth** credential.\n3. Activate the workflow. In SendRaven, add the webhook's production URL under **Webhooks**, for **inbound**.\n4. Paste the signing secret, `whsec_` included, into a **Crypto** credential on *Compute expected signature*.\n5. Add your OpenAI credential and fill in *Settings*.\n\n### Customization tips\nConnect *Escalate to a person* to Slack or your helpdesk. Drop the approval hold once the drafts look right."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b0668127-07b1-53d0-be22-521d88d6693a",
